# A chapter that has to be laid out from scratch must not take the pair down with it
# (docs/pageflip.md section 7), LEFT half: it presses nothing and crosses the boundary because the
# right half did, which is the case that killed a device on the bench -- both halves building the
# same cold chapter at the same moment, each holding the radio's 60 KB.
#
# The harness reports a low free-heap figure for a window around that crossing. This instance never
# actually runs out of memory, and cannot: the check here is that the link goes down for the build
# and comes back afterwards with the pairing intact, not that the build then fits.
#
# It quits first, a few seconds ahead of the right half, so its own departure is not read as a
# silence in the right half's log.
log pageflip-heapbuild-left: start
expect_timeout 90000
expect Entering activity: Home
wait 800
tap confirm
expect Entering activity: EpubReader
expect peer present
wait 28000
screenshot /screenshots/pf-hb-left-00.bmp
wait 800
log pageflip-heapbuild-left: done
quit
